## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | js/smAgent.js | ⚠️ important the gh 1369 pathology stays reachable via sibling agent rework writers — no more agent rework stamps on shipped code overclaims the terminal guard itself is well built pure leaf fail open probe reuse but prterminalstate is referenced only in js smagent js — the other machine writers of agent rework still ignore merge state and each is the same defect class the ticket title names rework arming stamps agent rework on already merged prs 1 js postprreviewcomments js 122 142 — markforsmstoryrework called from runreworkleg at 2252 a review leg in flight at merge time concludes request changes and stamps agent rework on the now merged pr ticket rework on label then dispatches a rework leg against shipped code this is exactly the leg already flying race the 1368 family lives in 2 js pushreworkchanges js 2393 — rearmnooprework a rework lap concluding no op on a pr that merged mid leg re arms agent rework the next tick dispatches another dead leg 3 js smagent js fail validation re arm paths 468 472 5276 5288 a pr that merged while validation was red gets re armed on the merged head on the next tick each site is one prheadandlabels isterminalprstate probe away from closed — the helper already exists and is unit tested ask either extend the terminal guard to these writers in this pr or narrow the pr description claim to the three guarded paths and file the follow up ticket as written no more agent rework stamps … on shipped code reads as a class level fix that is not one yet |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/prTerminalState.js | 💡 suggestion cross reference the sibling terminal state helper isprbodyfrozen js common pullrequest js 203 217 already implements a near sibling decision — isprbodyfrozen merged true → frozen state closed merged completed → frozen plus the merge queue label check the two contracts legitimately differ body freeze vs rework terminality ado completed merge queue label vs github rest terminal only freeze by default vs fail open but nothing in either file says so a one line cross reference in this module s header e g sibling isprbodyfrozen in pullrequest js — different contract body freeze ado completed merge queue labels do not unify without reconciling those and the fail open doctrine would stop a future dedup pass from silently merging them and flipping one of the semantics most dangerously dropping the fail open behavior the arming paths rely on |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | js/unit-tests/test_smAgent.js | 💡 suggestion add the closed not merged replay for reconcile verdicts coverage is uneven across the three guarded writers the arm suites replay ac1 merged and ac2 closed not merged and the unit tests cover isterminalprstate closed false true — but this reconcile suite replays only merged true the closed not merged state is real at the writer level a closed pr can be reopened and the reconcile deliberately exits during that window next tick after reopen self heals one more replay with state closed merged false asserting capturedprlabelremoves length 0 no comment would pin the writer level behavior at parity with the arm side and guard the guard against a future refactor that special cases merged only |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

